Osang and I are just fans of pandesal,

258
00:12:23,665 --> 00:12:26,323
especially the six-pack abs!

259
00:12:27,413 --> 00:12:30,500
Hey, Pipay! Just admit
it, you kind of like him!

260
00:12:30,651 --> 00:12:31,678
No, I don’t.

261
00:12:31,703 --> 00:12:32,793
Maybe Pipay does.

262
00:12:33,178 --> 00:12:34,972
I just really want to
taste the pandesal!

263
00:12:36,163 --> 00:12:38,137
Hey! Oh, come on!

264
00:12:38,816 --> 00:12:39,632
Just admit it!

265
00:12:40,205 --> 00:12:41,411
Excuse me!

266
00:12:44,159 --> 00:12:47,748
Can someone help
carry this sack of rice?

267
00:12:49,438 --> 00:12:49,924
I got it!

268
00:12:49,949 --> 00:12:52,948
Try coming closer,
and I’ll kick you!

269
00:12:52,973 --> 00:12:53,914
O…kay.

270
00:12:53,939 --> 00:12:55,536
I’ll hang your intestines out to dry!

271
00:12:57,837 --> 00:12:58,884
Je…

272
00:12:59,104 --> 00:12:59,851
Oh, here he comes!

273
00:12:59,876 --> 00:13:00,728
That’s it?

274
00:13:00,753 --> 00:13:01,845
Can you handle it?

275
00:13:02,054 --> 00:13:03,605
- This?!
- Yes.

276
00:13:04,096 --> 00:13:05,322
I got this!

277
00:13:05,347 --> 00:13:06,340
Really?

278
00:13:06,737 --> 00:13:08,115
Wait, are you feeling sick?

279
00:13:08,245 --> 00:13:09,865
No, what are you
talking about?

280
00:13:10,223 --> 00:13:11,503
This is just how I am!

281
00:13:11,547 --> 00:13:13,503
Ah, okay. Maybe it’s
just heavy for you?

282
00:13:17,404 --> 00:13:18,470
Smells so good!

283
00:13:18,495 --> 00:13:19,668
You’re strong!

284
00:13:19,986 --> 00:13:21,553
This is so annoying!

285
00:13:21,578 --> 00:13:23,501
Ah, where should I drop
this off? Your house?

286
00:13:23,652 --> 00:13:25,498
Uh, no, yours.

287
00:13:26,337 --> 00:13:27,335
My house?

288
00:13:27,608 --> 00:13:28,902
Yeah, it’s a gift for you.

289
00:13:30,268 --> 00:13:31,741
Wow!

290
00:13:31,766 --> 00:13:33,528
That’s so nice
of you, thank you!

291
00:13:33,636 --> 00:13:38,855
Yes! Yes, so remember, okay?

292
00:13:40,347 --> 00:13:45,817
You’ll never go hungry with
me because rice… I like you.

293
00:13:49,909 --> 00:13:50,789
Thank you, huh?

294
00:13:51,163 --> 00:13:53,610
Oh, Chard! Take it to the house.

295
00:13:54,174 --> 00:13:55,112
Thanks, okay?

296
00:13:58,584 --> 00:13:59,976
What kind of restaurant is this?

297
00:14:02,216 --> 00:14:04,862
It’s so quiet! No noise, boring!

298
00:14:05,556 --> 00:14:06,564
What is this?

299
00:14:07,103 --> 00:14:09,643
Ah, Andres, just relax.

300
00:14:10,336 --> 00:14:12,343
Don’t mind us being here.

301
00:14:12,368 --> 00:14:13,749
Just pretend we’re not here.

302
00:14:14,134 --> 00:14:15,081
Anne, okay?

303
00:14:15,279 --> 00:14:16,275
Just act normal.

304
00:14:16,714 --> 00:14:17,541
Alright?

305
00:14:17,594 --> 00:14:18,507
Okay.

306
00:14:18,607 --> 00:14:19,347
Okay.

307
00:14:19,585 --> 00:14:20,273
Okay.

308
00:14:20,584 --> 00:14:21,253
Yeah.

309
00:14:21,278 --> 00:14:21,980
Okay?

310
00:14:22,039 --> 00:14:22,971
- Okay.
- Okay.

311
00:14:25,193 --> 00:14:27,213
Anne, how have you been?

312
00:14:27,865 --> 00:14:31,150
Oh, Anne? Wow, this one!

313
00:14:31,175 --> 00:14:31,390
Oh?

314
00:14:31,415 --> 00:14:35,207
She does nothing but
wait for texts from… Andres!

315
00:14:35,232 --> 00:14:35,885
Oh, really?

316
00:14:35,910 --> 00:14:37,617
She gets all giddy
when he texts!

317
00:14:37,816 --> 00:14:40,286
She waits for his
messages, replies right away,

318
00:14:40,311 --> 00:14:43,330
and stays up all night!
Sleep-deprived in the morning.

319
00:14:45,030 --> 00:14:45,995
That’s Anne for you!

320
00:14:46,254 --> 00:14:48,646
Oh, wow! You’re too
funny, Anne. Amazing, huh?

321
00:14:49,413 --> 00:14:50,613
Oh, Tso K. just replied.

322
00:14:51,488 --> 00:14:53,968
Andres, where do
you want to go later?

323
00:14:54,288 --> 00:14:54,740
Later?

324
00:14:54,765 --> 00:14:55,865
Oh, Andres!

325
00:14:56,191 --> 00:14:57,678
He only wants one thing –

326
00:14:58,004 --> 00:14:59,592
guaranteed, take
him to the park!

327
00:15:00,308 --> 00:15:01,477
He loves parks.

328
00:15:01,740 --> 00:15:03,473
Because, you know,
budget’s a bit tight.

329
00:15:03,767 --> 00:15:06,407
First, you buy snacks
from the sari-sari store.

330
00:15:06,833 --> 00:15:07,213
Right?

331
00:15:07,238 --> 00:15:08,390
Like those cheap chips.

332
00:15:08,736 --> 00:15:11,355
Then he’ll take you to the
park, and you’ll just chat there.

333
00:15:11,386 --> 00:15:13,619
And then, you know,
holding hands and all that.

334
00:15:14,279 --> 00:15:19,198
That’s it! Sounds good, right?

335
00:15:19,243 --> 00:15:19,902
Really?

336
00:15:19,929 --> 00:15:20,436
Yeah!

337
00:15:20,461 --> 00:15:21,193
To the park, really?

338
00:15:21,237 --> 00:15:22,811
Park, park it is!

339
00:15:23,545 --> 00:15:25,280
Mmm, park, huh?

340
00:15:25,305 --> 00:15:27,747
Yes, yes, yes, yes!

341
00:15:28,946 --> 00:15:32,419
Oh, wait! The café
Dad suggested!

342
00:15:32,483 --> 00:15:33,436
- Right?
- Park!

343
00:15:33,461 --> 00:15:34,001
Park.

344
00:15:34,026 --> 00:15:40,215
But wasn’t it at the café that
you said you first met Mom?

345
00:15:40,240 --> 00:15:41,003
Ahh!

346
00:15:41,028 --> 00:15:42,647
Aah! That’s actually fine!

347
00:15:42,672 --> 00:15:44,592
Didn’t you suggest
that back at home?

348
00:15:44,617 --> 00:15:44,937
I was there!

349
00:15:44,962 --> 00:15:47,261
Perfect date spot!

350
00:15:47,438 --> 00:15:49,205
Ah, okay! That’s true!

351
00:15:49,435 --> 00:15:51,648
Actually, there’s a
café at the park too!

352
00:15:51,673 --> 00:15:53,863
That works.
Didn’t think of that!

353
00:15:53,888 --> 00:15:54,958
- Hi, sir!
- Oh, hi!

354
00:15:54,983 --> 00:15:56,600
- Good morning!
- Hello, hello, hello, hello!

355
00:15:56,625 --> 00:15:57,926
What would you like to order?

356
00:15:58,053 --> 00:15:58,721
Huh?

357
00:15:58,746 --> 00:15:59,666
Your order!

358
00:15:59,691 --> 00:16:03,635
No, um… Andres,
go ahead and order.

359
00:16:03,660 --> 00:16:04,179
Can I?

360
00:16:04,204 --> 00:16:08,124
You’re the gentleman, you
should do the ordering, okay?

361
00:16:09,266 --> 00:16:12,444
Your budget’s
tight, so just get…

362
00:16:13,977 --> 00:16:15,957
one piece of chicken each.

363
00:16:16,030 --> 00:16:16,645
Okay.

364
00:16:16,670 --> 00:16:18,203
Just the value meal, alright?

365
00:16:18,296 --> 00:16:19,536
- Wait, wait.
- Why?

366
00:16:19,733 --> 00:16:22,193
You, order the
most expensive one,

367
00:16:22,810 --> 00:16:25,050
because you’re a
woman, and you deserve it.

368
00:16:25,075 --> 00:16:26,189
Get the most expensive dish.

369
00:16:27,208 --> 00:16:28,602
That’s not practical.

370
00:16:29,068 --> 00:16:32,038
If it’s expensive, sometimes
it just goes to waste.

371
00:16:32,205 --> 00:16:33,565
I won’t even finish it.

372
00:16:33,590 --> 00:16:36,306
What do you want
Andres to order?

373
00:16:36,548 --> 00:16:37,142
Just chicken.

374
00:16:37,167 --> 00:16:38,226
- How many?
- One piece.

375
00:16:38,251 --> 00:16:39,447
Make it four, make it four.

376
00:16:39,574 --> 00:16:42,753
Two each, and get
large everything.

377
00:16:42,928 --> 00:16:44,702
And add dessert.

378
00:16:44,928 --> 00:16:46,155
Right?
There’s extra dessert.

379
00:16:46,381 --> 00:16:48,801
Get that cake I
saw on the shelf.

380
00:16:48,981 --> 00:16:49,550
- That one!
- Yes, Sir.

381
00:16:49,575 --> 00:16:51,353
Bring the whole
thing here.

382
00:16:51,378 --> 00:16:53,734
Not the whole
thing, just one slice.

383
00:16:53,821 --> 00:16:54,904
Why just one slice?

384
00:16:54,929 --> 00:16:56,113
There are four of us.

385
00:16:56,138 --> 00:16:56,604
One slice only!

386
00:16:56,629 --> 00:16:59,828
Okay, sir! Sir, alright,
here’s the deal—

387
00:17:00,301 --> 00:17:03,507
Here’s a pen, here’s paper.

388
00:17:04,740 --> 00:17:07,146
Just write down your order,

389
00:17:07,232 --> 00:17:11,691
and call us when you’re
done being chaotic.

390
00:17:12,096 --> 00:17:12,845
Okay?

391
00:17:13,653 --> 00:17:14,449
Thank you.

392
00:17:18,095 --> 00:17:22,735
Oh my gosh! This is insane!

393
00:17:25,036 --> 00:17:28,056
Atasha, how are sales today?

394
00:17:28,866 --> 00:17:30,259
Still slow, Mom.

395
00:17:30,570 --> 00:17:31,860
Slow?

396
00:17:32,410 --> 00:17:35,403
Why are you the only
one manning the stall?

397
00:17:36,588 --> 00:17:38,435
Mmm, how?

398
00:17:38,810 --> 00:17:39,856
Look at them!

399
00:17:40,328 --> 00:17:44,374
They’re all busy… flirting.

400
00:17:45,706 --> 00:17:46,766
You know what, Je?

401
00:17:46,898 --> 00:17:48,625
- Yes?
- I like you.

402
00:17:48,650 --> 00:17:49,536
Oh!

403
00:17:49,564 --> 00:17:52,564
I know you’re
exhausted from working,

404
00:17:52,722 --> 00:17:56,182
so here, later,
during your break…

405
00:17:58,419 --> 00:17:59,091
Here!

406
00:17:59,116 --> 00:18:01,629
- I thought it was something else.
- A SpaKarl voucher!

407
00:18:01,727 --> 00:18:02,713
I thought it was
something else.

408
00:18:02,824 --> 00:18:04,211
- Yes, it’s free!
- Wow!

409
00:18:04,420 --> 00:18:05,980
- I’ll give you a massage later.
- All of this?!

410
00:18:06,258 --> 00:18:07,478
All of this is free?!

411
00:18:07,503 --> 00:18:10,561
Yes, during your
break! Later, okay?

412
00:18:10,586 --> 00:18:11,268
Later?

413
00:18:11,293 --> 00:18:12,605
- Mm-mm.
- Mariposa…

414
00:18:12,789 --> 00:18:13,302
Oh?

415
00:18:13,327 --> 00:18:14,985
I’m exhausted too.

416
00:18:15,658 --> 00:18:16,844
Then go to sleep!

417
00:18:16,875 --> 00:18:18,396
Why are you even here?

418
00:18:19,492 --> 00:18:20,565
I got sent to sleep.

419
00:18:20,631 --> 00:18:24,151
Really? Wow! Fancy!

420
00:18:24,350 --> 00:18:25,737
What time’s the massage?

421
00:18:26,025 --> 00:18:26,900
What time?

422
00:18:26,925 --> 00:18:30,605
What time’s your break? Around five?

423
00:18:30,684 --> 00:18:31,651
- Five!
- Five?

424
00:18:31,676 --> 00:18:33,910
Five!
Uh, what time is it now?

425
00:18:33,935 --> 00:18:35,168
Ah, 4:30?

426
00:18:35,265 --> 00:18:36,738
- 4:30!
- Yes.

427
00:18:36,875 --> 00:18:41,350
4:30 means
your break isn’t over yet.

428
00:18:41,628 --> 00:18:42,734
Back to work!

429
00:18:42,759 --> 00:18:44,316
- Work time!
- Let’s go! Come on!

430
00:18:44,982 --> 00:18:47,114
- Come here!
- Bye, Je!

431
00:18:47,139 --> 00:18:47,519
Bye!

432
00:18:47,544 --> 00:18:49,017
See you later, Je!

433
00:18:50,247 --> 00:18:51,294
Out of the way!

434
00:18:54,597 --> 00:18:55,460
Yuck!

435
00:18:58,418 --> 00:18:59,283
Mmm, what?

436
00:19:00,004 --> 00:19:00,902
Back to work.

437
00:19:04,479 --> 00:19:06,418
- Badong, come here!
- Yeah?

438
00:19:07,389 --> 00:19:09,409
Ugh, seriously? Isn’t this the
same thing you always wear?!

439
00:19:10,177 --> 00:19:11,787
I’m selling it too, so we
can earn a little extra!

440
00:19:11,812 --> 00:19:13,321
Huh? Extra income?

441
00:19:13,527 --> 00:19:14,940
It still smells like formalin!

442
00:19:15,740 --> 00:19:16,726
Are you insane?!

443
00:19:16,751 --> 00:19:17,676
It’s freshly washed!

444
00:19:17,701 --> 00:19:18,555
Freshly washed?

445
00:19:18,628 --> 00:19:19,055
Yeah!

446
00:19:19,097 --> 00:19:20,323
Well, you should have taken
a bath while you were at it.

447
00:19:21,338 --> 00:19:23,718
And instead of selling clothes,
maybe use the money to buy food!

448
00:19:23,962 --> 00:19:25,041
Look at yourself,

449
00:19:25,086 --> 00:19:26,546
our dinner plates
are thicker than you!

450
00:19:27,770 --> 00:19:28,938
Unbelievable!

451
00:19:34,571 --> 00:19:35,624
Oh!

452
00:19:38,011 --> 00:19:41,137
Mariposa, you’re glowing today!

453
00:19:41,162 --> 00:19:44,353
Oh my gosh, thank you
so much, Boss Beauty!

454
00:19:44,378 --> 00:19:45,418
But you know what?

455
00:19:45,443 --> 00:19:49,145
You are too! Your
aura is different today!

456
00:19:49,470 --> 00:19:50,830
Oh, don’t mention it!

457
00:19:50,861 --> 00:19:53,741
But you… looks like someone’s
making you happy, huh?

458
00:19:53,766 --> 00:19:56,181
Oh my gosh, yes!

459
00:19:56,261 --> 00:19:56,848
Really?

460
00:19:56,873 --> 00:19:57,912
Mmm-hmm!

461
00:19:57,937 --> 00:20:07,098
Someone sexy,
hardworking, and manly!

462
00:20:09,635 --> 00:20:11,081
Ahh! But what about you?

463
00:20:11,106 --> 00:20:14,210
Well, same here.

464
00:20:15,317 --> 00:20:16,784
Someone hardworking…

465
00:20:16,884 --> 00:20:17,744
Ah!

466
00:20:17,905 --> 00:20:20,918
Sexy, and manly!

467
00:20:20,944 --> 00:20:24,639
Ah! Wait a second…
the same person?!

468
00:20:25,036 --> 00:20:26,609
Oh wow, yeah!

469
00:20:27,230 --> 00:20:30,200
Let’s say the name
at the same time!

470
00:20:30,301 --> 00:20:30,939
Alright.

471
00:20:30,964 --> 00:20:31,491
Okay.

472
00:20:31,516 --> 00:20:32,931
- At the count of three.
- Okay.

473
00:20:33,319 --> 00:20:35,719
One…Two…Three!

474
00:20:35,918 --> 00:20:37,177
- It’s Je!
- It’s Je!

475
00:20:37,485 --> 00:20:40,530
Oh my god!

476
00:20:42,394 --> 00:20:47,570
So, does this mean we’re
going from sisters to rivals?!

477
00:20:48,272 --> 00:20:51,485
Well, let’s see who wins!

478
00:20:53,378 --> 00:20:55,491
Oh, really?

479
00:20:56,270 --> 00:20:59,170
You’re challenging me?

480
00:21:00,098 --> 00:21:01,103
Ha!

481
00:21:01,128 --> 00:21:03,435
I’m not even threatened!

482
00:21:05,385 --> 00:21:06,632
Big word!

483
00:21:06,872 --> 00:21:08,625
You don’t even know
how to spell “threatened”!

484
00:21:08,775 --> 00:21:10,521
You think so?!

485
00:21:11,802 --> 00:21:12,829
With a “w”!

486
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:15,126
Idiot!

487
00:21:19,397 --> 00:21:22,327
Oh, Andres, where are they?

488
00:21:22,352 --> 00:21:23,742
My BFFs?

489
00:21:24,369 --> 00:21:25,478
Bathroom.

490
00:21:25,684 --> 00:21:26,711
Oh, okay.

491
00:21:31,634 --> 00:21:32,867
Weren’t you guys
supposed to go somewhere?

492
00:21:33,497 --> 00:21:35,877
Oh, this is great! Good news!

493
00:21:36,257 --> 00:21:37,313
Canceled!

494
00:21:37,934 --> 00:21:40,994
So now, I can join you guys.

495
00:21:41,758 --> 00:21:42,784
Isn’t it great?

496
00:21:43,230 --> 00:21:47,307
Perfect timing! We get to bond!

497
00:21:47,738 --> 00:21:48,610
Dad…

498
00:21:48,635 --> 00:21:49,935
- Yes, Andres?
- No offense, okay?

499
00:21:50,267 --> 00:21:51,011
Of course.

500
00:21:51,036 --> 00:21:53,423
But… this kinda
turned into a bad date.

501
00:21:53,980 --> 00:21:55,340
- B-bad date?
- Yes.

502
00:21:55,706 --> 00:21:57,993
No… but… why?

503
00:21:58,179 --> 00:21:59,593
How did this become
a bad date?

504
00:21:59,618 --> 00:22:02,743
Isn’t it better that I’m here? I
mean, I can give you tips, right?

505
00:22:03,691 --> 00:22:04,764
No, because, Dad…

506
00:22:06,117 --> 00:22:07,597
why are you and Tso K even here?

507
00:22:07,922 --> 00:22:11,066
To… you know… support you.

508
00:22:11,347 --> 00:22:12,263
Is that wrong?

509
00:22:12,288 --> 00:22:13,602
Not really, Dad.

510
00:22:14,456 --> 00:22:15,943
I get it, you have your ways.

511
00:22:16,023 --> 00:22:16,895
Mmm-hmm.

512
00:22:17,075 --> 00:22:19,142
But I have my own way too,

513
00:22:19,167 --> 00:22:21,199
and I can’t do anything
because you guys are here.

514
00:22:21,391 --> 00:22:22,485
Wait, wait, wait.

515
00:22:22,656 --> 00:22:24,963
Are you saying… I’m the
one in the wrong here?

516
00:22:24,988 --> 00:22:27,520
No… no… it’s not
like that, Dad.

517
00:22:27,753 --> 00:22:29,493
No, it sounds like you’re saying…

518
00:22:29,518 --> 00:22:30,817
It’s like…you sound like…

519
00:22:31,805 --> 00:22:33,425
Oh, thank god!

520
00:22:33,518 --> 00:22:34,366
That felt great!

521
00:22:34,391 --> 00:22:35,751
I’m done in the bathroom!

522
00:22:36,613 --> 00:22:38,066
Time for round two.

523
00:22:38,846 --> 00:22:40,048
Menu, please!

524
00:22:43,662 --> 00:22:44,654
Miss!

525
00:22:45,533 --> 00:22:46,373
Hold on…

526
00:22:46,743 --> 00:22:49,116
There!
I’d like to order again.

527
00:22:56,091 --> 00:22:57,660
Hi, Je!

528
00:22:58,241 --> 00:23:01,700
Je, I’m so glad you made it!

529
00:23:02,109 --> 00:23:03,669
Um, promise,

530
00:23:04,162 --> 00:23:06,968
I’ll make this quick so when
you get back to the bakery,

531
00:23:07,361 --> 00:23:10,191
you’ll be refreshed, okay?

532
00:23:10,527 --> 00:23:12,433
I’ll start now!

533
00:23:15,699 --> 00:23:18,471
Wait, Je… your biceps…

534
00:23:19,045 --> 00:23:20,131
they’re shrinking.

535
00:23:21,877 --> 00:23:26,049
And your back…

536
00:23:26,744 --> 00:23:28,271
looks like it’s caving in?

537
00:23:29,128 --> 00:23:31,321
Is the bakery that stressful?

538
00:23:31,667 --> 00:23:33,674
You seriously need to unwind!

539
00:23:36,133 --> 00:23:38,759
And wait…

540
00:23:39,322 --> 00:23:40,716
your pandesal,

541
00:23:41,481 --> 00:23:45,850
it’s turning into one big monay!

542
00:23:46,563 --> 00:23:49,493
And your hair…

543
00:23:49,518 --> 00:23:51,351
looks like it’s thinning!

544
00:23:51,773 --> 00:23:54,513
Ahh! What’s
happening to the baker?!

545
00:23:54,538 --> 00:23:55,522
- Hold on…
- Ahh!

546
00:23:55,911 --> 00:23:56,659
- Wait a minute!
- Ahh!

547
00:23:56,684 --> 00:23:58,844
You’re going too
far with the insults!

548
00:23:58,869 --> 00:24:00,075
You’re not Je!

549
00:24:00,119 --> 00:24:00,779
I know.

550
00:24:00,804 --> 00:24:02,161
Then why… why are you here?

551
00:24:02,186 --> 00:24:03,485
He’s supposed to be here!

552
00:24:03,510 --> 00:24:04,216
Je’s not here.

553
00:24:04,241 --> 00:24:05,466
I made sure of it!

554
00:24:05,850 --> 00:24:07,417
Because Je is mine!

555
00:24:07,505 --> 00:24:09,265
Oh, no. Je is mine!

556
00:24:09,290 --> 00:24:10,436
- Je is mine!
- No, he’s mine!

557
00:24:10,461 --> 00:24:11,647
- He’s mine!
- He’s mine!

558
00:24:11,672 --> 00:24:12,524
- He’s mine!
- I said, mine!

559
00:24:12,549 --> 00:24:14,234
Hold up,
Boss Beauty, Mariposa!

560
00:24:14,259 --> 00:24:15,036
Oh, Je…

561
00:24:15,061 --> 00:24:17,125
Enough! Stop it!

562
00:24:18,184 --> 00:24:19,604
Make love, not war.

563
00:24:20,046 --> 00:24:20,966
Okay?

564
00:24:21,744 --> 00:24:22,394
Oh!

565
00:24:22,419 --> 00:24:23,485
Are you okay?

566
00:24:23,545 --> 00:24:25,373
I’m about to die on this couch!

567
00:24:27,144 --> 00:24:29,371
It’s your last scene to
shoot, and you almost died!

568
00:24:30,303 --> 00:24:32,083
- Je, you’re mine, okay?
- Je is mine.

569
00:24:32,108 --> 00:24:33,656
- Je is mine.
- No, shut up.

570
00:24:33,681 --> 00:24:34,998
- Je is mine!
- Stop it! Je is mine!

571
00:24:35,023 --> 00:24:37,425
He’s mine! Je is mine!

572
00:24:37,646 --> 00:24:38,711
Je is mine!

573
00:24:41,939 --> 00:24:43,679
Anne's taking forever
in the bathroom!

574
00:24:43,704 --> 00:24:44,391
Yeah, right?

575
00:24:44,416 --> 00:24:45,556
She's been in there
for a while now.

576
00:24:49,544 --> 00:24:52,091
Uh, Dad… I have a call.

577
00:24:52,415 --> 00:24:53,426
I'll just step out for a bit.

578
00:24:53,698 --> 00:24:55,112
Okay! Go ahead.
Of course, of course!

579
00:24:55,245 --> 00:24:56,153
Alright.

580
00:24:56,178 --> 00:24:57,678
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

581
00:25:07,696 --> 00:25:09,069
You think she took
a shower in there?

582
00:25:09,589 --> 00:25:10,610
You know, Je,

583
00:25:11,257 --> 00:25:16,104
I called you here to
help with the bakery,

584
00:25:16,436 --> 00:25:19,543
not to cause trouble
in the neighborhood!

585
00:25:19,916 --> 00:25:21,149
That’s right, Je!

586
00:25:22,108 --> 00:25:22,917
Je?

587
00:25:23,272 --> 00:25:24,057
Je!

588
00:25:24,432 --> 00:25:25,340
- Je!
- Hey!

589
00:25:25,365 --> 00:25:26,072
Wake up!

590
00:25:26,090 --> 00:25:27,223
Sorry, I dozed off.

591
00:25:29,863 --> 00:25:31,890
Lola, no, I heard you, Lola.

592
00:25:32,172 --> 00:25:35,860
But it’s not my fault
if it runs in our family

593
00:25:35,977 --> 00:25:37,424
to be totally smitten!

594
00:25:37,490 --> 00:25:41,849
Oh really? You sure?

595
00:25:42,349 --> 00:25:44,042
Seriously?

596
00:25:45,135 --> 00:25:46,448
Just a little fainting
here and there.

597
00:25:47,165 --> 00:25:48,265
What about you?

598
00:25:48,771 --> 00:25:50,918
Well, just slightly.

599
00:25:51,644 --> 00:25:52,679
Still revivable.

600
00:25:52,704 --> 00:25:53,537
Like this!

601
00:25:54,181 --> 00:25:55,322
Je, I can’t breathe!

602
00:25:55,347 --> 00:25:56,707
Give me mouth-to-mouth!

603
00:25:57,193 --> 00:25:58,296
Give me mouth-to-mouth!

604
00:25:58,321 --> 00:26:01,061
Oh? Whoa, whoa,
whoa! Hold on, hold on!

605
00:26:01,086 --> 00:26:01,900
What mouth-to-mouth?!

606
00:26:01,925 --> 00:26:03,705
Don’t use those to block me!

607
00:26:03,926 --> 00:26:05,159
Half of that is just foam!

608
00:26:05,184 --> 00:26:06,028
Go ahead, go over there!

609
00:26:06,053 --> 00:26:07,118
Listen to yourself!

610
00:26:07,143 --> 00:26:09,616
I saw her stuffing trash in there!

611
00:26:09,641 --> 00:26:11,454
It’s not trash, girl! It’s socks!

612
00:26:12,491 --> 00:26:14,378
Hey, cut it out, hold on!

613
00:26:14,403 --> 00:26:15,932
We’ve got a bigger problem—

614
00:26:15,957 --> 00:26:20,046
we haven’t even hit
today’s sales target yet!

615
00:26:20,071 --> 00:26:21,168
Right?

616
00:26:21,206 --> 00:26:22,479
What are we gonna do?

617
00:26:22,986 --> 00:26:24,526
Mom, I have an idea…

618
00:26:24,551 --> 00:26:25,251
What is it?

619
00:26:25,276 --> 00:26:26,603
And it’s not just
a random thought.

620
00:26:28,573 --> 00:26:31,131
Okay, since this
already happened, okay…

621
00:26:31,156 --> 00:26:34,280
I found an idea we can use

622
00:26:34,380 --> 00:26:37,265
to make money here at
Bake Haus of U, okay?

623
00:26:37,290 --> 00:26:38,517
- Idea?
- Yes.

624
00:26:38,542 --> 00:26:39,845
What’s this idea?

625
00:26:39,870 --> 00:26:44,932
Yes… since there are a lot
of gossipers hanging around,

626
00:26:45,092 --> 00:26:47,898
all the nosy neighbors
here in Barangay Singko,

627
00:26:47,923 --> 00:26:49,352
we’ll make this
place their go-to spot.

628
00:26:49,764 --> 00:26:53,758
While they discuss all the drama,

629
00:26:53,783 --> 00:26:56,512
they’ll have snacks
here at Bake Haus of U—

630
00:26:56,569 --> 00:26:59,810
because this is now fez-to-fez!

631
00:27:04,003 --> 00:27:05,025
You know…

632
00:27:05,897 --> 00:27:08,204
it’s been like fifteen minutes,
and they’re still not back.

633
00:27:10,021 --> 00:27:10,730
Yeah, right?

634
00:27:10,755 --> 00:27:12,495
Didn’t they just go
to the bathroom?

635
00:27:13,061 --> 00:27:14,675
But I’m more curious about Anne!

636
00:27:14,999 --> 00:27:16,398
- She’s taking so long!
- Right?

637
00:27:16,429 --> 00:27:18,653
She probably left
her intestines in there.

638
00:27:18,993 --> 00:27:21,513
I knew it… Andres said he had a call.

639
00:27:21,826 --> 00:27:22,924
It’s been fifteen minutes!

640
00:27:25,261 --> 00:27:25,761
Hi, sir!

641
00:27:25,786 --> 00:27:26,891
- Hi!
- Hi!

642
00:27:27,010 --> 00:27:27,444
What?

643
00:27:27,469 --> 00:27:28,342
- Your bill.
- Our what–?

644
00:27:28,966 --> 00:27:30,126
- Bill?
- Yes, sir!

645
00:27:31,215 --> 00:27:32,275
Oh. Wait, hold on!

646
00:27:32,547 --> 00:27:34,693
Oh. Wait, hold on! Andres
is supposed to pay for this.

647
00:27:35,679 --> 00:27:36,146
That’s right.

648
00:27:36,221 --> 00:27:38,514
Wait… wait, wait, wait.

649
00:27:38,645 --> 00:27:39,998
Oh no, sir!

650
00:27:40,023 --> 00:27:41,627
Wait a minute.
Do you have any cash?

651
00:27:41,652 --> 00:27:42,596
- Me?
- Sir…

652
00:27:43,675 --> 00:27:44,848
I have my purse.

653
00:27:45,597 --> 00:27:46,777
Maybe you can
cover it first?

654
00:27:46,802 --> 00:27:48,156
I didn’t bring it,
it’s just full of coins.

655
00:27:48,181 --> 00:27:49,289
Maybe you can cover
it for now?

656
00:27:49,314 --> 00:27:50,458
- Sir…
- Ah, yes?

657
00:27:50,483 --> 00:27:54,869
This trick of yours, sir…
your little gimmicks?

658
00:27:54,894 --> 00:27:56,029
They’re so outdated!

659
00:27:56,155 --> 00:27:57,768
Just like you, sir!

660
00:27:58,726 --> 00:27:59,740
Ugh!

661
00:27:59,981 --> 00:28:02,774
You ordered so much,
and now you can’t even pay!

662
00:28:03,949 --> 00:28:07,579
Sir, just pay up so
we can move on, sir.

663
00:28:08,112 --> 00:28:10,005
No… we shouldn’t be paying.

664
00:28:10,030 --> 00:28:11,676
We’re just waiting
for his son.

665
00:28:11,701 --> 00:28:13,333
Alright, has everyone
bought something?

666
00:28:13,597 --> 00:28:14,597
Yes!

667
00:28:14,622 --> 00:28:17,493
Okay, then let’s
start deciding on the

668
00:28:17,538 --> 00:28:20,157
Baker Who’s No Longer a Bestie.

669
00:28:20,195 --> 00:28:22,408
Alright, starting with Boss Beauty.

670
00:28:22,433 --> 00:28:24,783
Here’s our first question, okay…

671
00:28:25,114 --> 00:28:28,726
what can you say about
Mariposa’s statement that

672
00:28:29,219 --> 00:28:31,426
friendships don’t matter
when it comes to guys?

673
00:28:32,791 --> 00:28:33,998
You said that?!

674
00:28:34,098 --> 00:28:34,652
I didn’t say that!

675
00:28:34,677 --> 00:28:35,496
You did?!

676
00:28:35,521 --> 00:28:36,307
I never said that!

677
00:28:36,332 --> 00:28:37,537
Wait, wait, wait!

678
00:28:37,562 --> 00:28:38,399
I never said that!

679
00:28:38,424 --> 00:28:39,772
What?! You think
I’d be scared of you?!

680
00:28:39,797 --> 00:28:41,529
You even dragged those folks
from Silang, Cavite into this!

681
00:28:41,591 --> 00:28:43,231
Friends of Direk Danni?!

682
00:28:43,256 --> 00:28:43,889
Yes!

683
00:28:43,914 --> 00:28:45,239
What, are they
auditioning for VivaMax?!

684
00:28:45,264 --> 00:28:45,983
Oh, that’s them?!

685
00:28:46,008 --> 00:28:46,706
Could be!

686
00:28:47,767 --> 00:28:49,481
So, your answer is…?

687
00:28:50,282 --> 00:28:51,221
Well,

688
00:28:51,829 --> 00:28:53,735
according to the
rules of friendship,

689
00:28:55,185 --> 00:28:57,432
first come, first served.

690
00:28:57,837 --> 00:29:01,416
Whoever sees him first gets him!

691
00:29:01,712 --> 00:29:03,631
And I was the first to lay eyes on Je!

692
00:29:03,764 --> 00:29:05,118
If you had any decency,

693
00:29:05,191 --> 00:29:07,104
you would've backed
off immediately, right?!

694
00:29:07,361 --> 00:29:08,176
Oh!

695
00:29:08,201 --> 00:29:09,634
Somebody hold me back!
Hold me back!

696
00:29:09,659 --> 00:29:12,333
Okay, here’s the next question…

697
00:29:12,371 --> 00:29:15,732
Mariposa, what do you
have to say about this

698
00:29:15,757 --> 00:29:16,769
“friendship over” situation?

699
00:29:17,823 --> 00:29:19,223
All I have to say is—

700
00:29:19,662 --> 00:29:22,795
save the best for last.

701
00:29:23,532 --> 00:29:25,839
Sure, you were first,

702
00:29:26,092 --> 00:29:29,445
but I’m the better one!

703
00:29:29,470 --> 00:29:31,170
Wow! You’re really
pushing it now!

704
00:29:31,195 --> 00:29:33,829
Yeah! You might be
prettier, but they’re older!

705
00:29:36,355 --> 00:29:40,221
What’s your comment
on this whole issue?

706
00:29:40,271 --> 00:29:41,296
You know what,

707
00:29:41,549 --> 00:29:46,146
I don’t even know
how we got here,

708
00:29:46,654 --> 00:29:53,964
but I really think friends
shouldn’t be fighting over a guy.

709
00:29:54,577 --> 00:29:55,609
Right?

710
00:29:55,758 --> 00:29:58,704
Right, right, right!
That’s right, right?

711
00:29:59,015 --> 00:29:59,528
Right!

712
00:29:59,604 --> 00:30:01,630
Alright, okay!

713
00:30:01,655 --> 00:30:04,014
Now, Lola Maxi, of course,
the most beautiful of all.

714
00:30:04,039 --> 00:30:05,504
What do you think?

715
00:30:06,828 --> 00:30:09,034
Honestly, nothing much.

716
00:30:09,265 --> 00:30:12,902
I’m just happy that it’s
been proven once again—

717
00:30:12,927 --> 00:30:15,001
Our family is just
naturally irresistible!

718
00:30:15,026 --> 00:30:15,648
Right?!

719
00:30:15,673 --> 00:30:16,439
Irresistible?

720
00:30:16,464 --> 00:30:18,853
Let’s give her a
round of applause!

721
00:30:18,878 --> 00:30:19,900
Thank you so much!

722
00:30:19,925 --> 00:30:22,034
Okay, now… Kuya Je,
what’s your comment—

723
00:30:22,059 --> 00:30:23,159
Wait, I have something to say!

724
00:30:23,184 --> 00:30:24,190
No, no, you’re not
saying anything.

725
00:30:24,215 --> 00:30:25,245
Stay right here.

726
00:30:25,270 --> 00:30:25,717
Huh?

727
00:30:25,742 --> 00:30:27,674
Wow, impressive.
Kuya Je, go ahead.

728
00:30:27,778 --> 00:30:28,826
Ah, thank you.

729
00:30:30,806 --> 00:30:33,345
First of all, I’d like
to thank everyone.

730
00:30:38,579 --> 00:30:42,839
But for now, my focus
is really on my career.

731
00:30:43,722 --> 00:30:47,174
So, especially here at the
bakery, that’s my priority.

732
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:55,226
To settle this and end the
fight, let’s just have a group hug.

733
00:30:55,356 --> 00:30:58,720
- There we go!
- Group hug! Group hug!

734
00:31:07,939 --> 00:31:11,271
If I see Anne and Andres,

735
00:31:11,512 --> 00:31:12,598
they better be ready

736
00:31:12,904 --> 00:31:15,017
because they’re really
in trouble with me.

737
00:31:15,252 --> 00:31:16,932
Yeah, but you know,

738
00:31:17,149 --> 00:31:19,216
I kind of get what
Andres was saying.

739
00:31:19,273 --> 00:31:20,960
Maybe we should
just let them be.

740
00:31:21,355 --> 00:31:24,634
They’re not doing
anything wrong, right?

741
00:31:24,727 --> 00:31:26,194
- You know, BFF…
- Mmm?

742
00:31:26,440 --> 00:31:27,727
- To be honest…
- Mmm?

743
00:31:28,008 --> 00:31:30,528
I actually approve of Andres.

744
00:31:31,076 --> 00:31:34,036
But of course, I
can’t help but worry—

745
00:31:34,551 --> 00:31:35,911
she’s my niece, after all.

746
00:31:37,339 --> 00:31:38,439
Of course. But you know,

747
00:31:38,663 --> 00:31:40,457
I understand where
you’re coming from.

748
00:31:40,951 --> 00:31:43,071
It’s just that… they’re old enough.

749
00:31:43,417 --> 00:31:45,783
But at the same time,
they’re still young.

750
00:31:46,354 --> 00:31:49,424
What I mean is, they
know what they’re doing.

751
00:31:49,704 --> 00:31:52,451
And first of all, it’s not like
we didn’t raise them well, right?

752
00:31:53,470 --> 00:31:55,490
That’s true, you have a point.

753
00:31:56,109 --> 00:31:57,656
Right? So, it’s fine!

754
00:31:59,573 --> 00:32:00,579
There they are!

755
00:32:01,192 --> 00:32:03,191
Look at them… I swear,
I’m gonna hurt those two!

756
00:32:03,216 --> 00:32:04,814
- Wait, wait!
- Huh?

757
00:32:04,839 --> 00:32:05,417
Wait!

758
00:32:05,442 --> 00:32:06,826
We just talked about this!

759
00:32:07,299 --> 00:32:08,899
I just said to relax, didn’t I?

760
00:32:08,943 --> 00:32:11,284
I’m mad because they
made us spend money!

761
00:32:11,309 --> 00:32:12,893
Well, you ate too!

762
00:32:13,473 --> 00:32:14,379
Me?!

763
00:32:14,657 --> 00:32:15,706
It’s fine now!

764
00:32:16,077 --> 00:32:16,830
They’re making me mad!

765
00:32:16,855 --> 00:32:18,727
Let it go, it’s fine.

766
00:32:18,752 --> 00:32:20,044
Come on, let’s just go home.

767
00:32:20,069 --> 00:32:21,019
Let’s go, let’s go.

768
00:32:21,044 --> 00:32:23,950
A date? Come on, man, there’s no—

769
00:32:23,975 --> 00:32:24,958
Date? With—

770
00:32:24,983 --> 00:32:26,076
Don’t say date!

771
00:32:26,101 --> 00:32:27,497
What do you take me for, gay?

772
00:32:27,522 --> 00:32:29,136
- Don’t make me gay!
- I didn’t say anything!

773
00:32:29,246 --> 00:32:29,679
No...

774
00:32:29,704 --> 00:32:31,488
But, you just –

775
00:32:31,606 --> 00:32:32,342
A date?

776
00:32:32,367 --> 00:32:33,507
Then why are you
holding me?

777
00:32:33,532 --> 00:32:34,520
Fine, I’ll let go!

778
00:32:35,033 --> 00:32:36,446
I just said let’s go home.

779
00:32:36,566 --> 00:32:38,153
Dude, why are you panicking?

780
00:32:38,178 --> 00:32:40,083
I’m not panicking,
I’m just surprised!

781
00:32:40,128 --> 00:32:42,280
No, I’m just saying,
you’re holding me.

782
00:32:42,285 --> 00:32:44,797
I thought you were about
to say we’re going on a date.

783
00:32:44,822 --> 00:32:49,084
But we can totally go on
a date—as friends, I mean—

784
00:32:49,178 --> 00:32:50,705
- See!
- Like the good old days!

785
00:32:50,730 --> 00:32:51,501
Exactly!

786
00:32:51,509 --> 00:32:53,055
Alright, fine! Holding
hands is okay now!

787
00:32:53,641 --> 00:32:54,612
Let’s go!

788
00:32:54,981 --> 00:32:56,850
Just holding hands.
Just holding hands.

789
00:32:56,875 --> 00:32:58,315
It’s fine! Let's go!

790
00:32:58,334 --> 00:32:59,448
This feels kind of weird?

791
00:32:59,473 --> 00:33:01,517
What’s weird?
Your arm is just twisted.

792
00:33:02,714 --> 00:33:03,554
Oh, there!

793
00:33:03,579 --> 00:33:06,473
See! That’s what I’m
saying! Alright, let’s go!

794
00:33:06,546 --> 00:33:09,179
Yeah, just walking like real bros.

795
00:33:09,246 --> 00:33:10,260
That’s what I like!

796
00:33:10,285 --> 00:33:12,058
Yeah, now stop being grumpy.

797
00:33:14,542 --> 00:33:17,388
Andres, how was
your date with Anne?

798
00:33:17,782 --> 00:33:21,055
Yeah, Dad, thanks so
much for letting us go.

799
00:33:21,182 --> 00:33:23,082
Of course! Did you have fun?

800
00:33:23,272 --> 00:33:24,172
Of course!

801
00:33:24,745 --> 00:33:25,652
You know what I did?

802
00:33:25,677 --> 00:33:26,367
- What?
- Oh?

803
00:33:26,392 --> 00:33:29,012
I did everything you taught me!

804
00:33:29,912 --> 00:33:31,518
- The things I taught you?!
- What?

805
00:33:31,543 --> 00:33:32,314
I didn’t teach you anything!

806
00:33:32,339 --> 00:33:33,774
What exactly did you
teach him?

807
00:33:33,799 --> 00:33:34,927
How to love!

808
00:33:35,033 --> 00:33:36,846
- That’s right!
- Nice!

809
00:33:36,871 --> 00:33:38,408
Is that true, Andres?

810
00:33:39,048 --> 00:33:39,707
Yes, Mom.

811
00:33:39,732 --> 00:33:40,932
Yes, Mom!

812
00:33:40,957 --> 00:33:44,267
Good boy, good boy!
Yeah, yeah!

813
00:33:44,292 --> 00:33:45,220
Now, hold on.

814
00:33:45,397 --> 00:33:48,043
How’s the business doing, Atasha?

815
00:33:48,068 --> 00:33:51,300
Good news, we’re making
a lot of money now, Mom!

816
00:33:51,325 --> 00:33:52,779
Alright!

817
00:33:52,804 --> 00:33:54,870
It’s all thanks to Fez to Fez!

818
00:33:57,005 --> 00:33:58,152
Fabulous!

819
00:33:58,822 --> 00:33:59,869
Thank you!

820
00:34:00,477 --> 00:34:01,056
You’re amazing!

821
00:34:01,081 --> 00:34:03,277
Tash, you’re really
something else. Good job!

822
00:34:03,369 --> 00:34:04,683
Thank you so much.

823
00:34:05,091 --> 00:34:07,334
That’s the way to do it—no stress,

824
00:34:07,359 --> 00:34:09,572
and you even found a
way to make things work.

825
00:34:09,847 --> 00:34:11,944
- Yeah. No problem.
- Thank you!

826
00:34:11,969 --> 00:34:15,598
Because what’s
really important is

827
00:34:15,687 --> 00:34:18,387
that everyone makes up.

828
00:34:18,606 --> 00:34:24,058
You two, you guys,
and Kuya Chard and I.

829
00:34:24,303 --> 00:34:25,360
Right?

830
00:34:25,444 --> 00:34:28,204
- There you go!
- That’s right!

831
00:34:28,871 --> 00:34:30,296
There was never
really a problem.

832
00:34:30,321 --> 00:34:31,704
Actually, Tito Aga, sorry…

833
00:34:31,729 --> 00:34:33,176
there was no issue at all.

834
00:34:33,201 --> 00:34:34,387
I don’t even know
what happened.

835
00:34:34,417 --> 00:34:36,079
I just wore a
tank top, that’s it!

836
00:34:36,104 --> 00:34:38,514
I wasn’t even doing anything!

837
00:34:40,729 --> 00:34:41,789
You want a tank top?

838
00:34:41,973 --> 00:34:43,387
I used to wear tank
tops, you know?

839
00:34:43,595 --> 00:34:44,075
Oh no!

840
00:34:44,100 --> 00:34:44,808
Oh?

841
00:34:47,062 --> 00:34:49,539
If it’s a white tank
top you’re looking for,

842
00:34:50,837 --> 00:34:51,752
here I am.

843
00:34:51,964 --> 00:34:52,886
Oh wow!

844
00:34:53,465 --> 00:34:56,431
Oh, Chard, can
you please change?

845
00:34:56,456 --> 00:34:58,142
I’m so sick of your outfit.

846
00:34:58,669 --> 00:35:00,282
Lola, calm down.

847
00:35:00,307 --> 00:35:00,546
Oh!

848
00:35:00,571 --> 00:35:02,476
Relax. It’s just me!

849
00:35:03,136 --> 00:35:05,282
So, Boss Beauty, Mariposa,

850
00:35:05,804 --> 00:35:08,017
if Je doesn’t
choose either of you,

851
00:35:08,042 --> 00:35:11,520
I’m here to catch
you when you… fall.

852
00:35:11,804 --> 00:35:13,984
Oh! Did you guys hear that?

853
00:35:14,699 --> 00:35:16,086
- Hey, hey, hey, hey!
- I’m good now.

854
00:35:16,532 --> 00:35:18,539
You! Don’t mess with me!

855
00:35:18,564 --> 00:35:20,558
I don’t go for mini pinschers!

856
00:35:21,348 --> 00:35:22,268
Mini pinscher.

857
00:35:22,293 --> 00:35:24,205
And besides, I’m good—I’m
allergic to chihuahuas!

858
00:35:26,711 --> 00:35:28,191
Stop fighting over me!

859
00:35:28,216 --> 00:35:29,335
We’re not fighting
over you!

860
00:35:29,360 --> 00:35:30,779
We’re not fighting
over you! Go home!

861
00:35:30,804 --> 00:35:31,745
We're good!

862
00:35:31,770 --> 00:35:33,446
One at a time!

863
00:35:33,471 --> 00:35:34,493
What now? What now?

864
00:35:34,518 --> 00:35:35,911
- One at a time!
- Flex, flex!
